    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **26 run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the three directly affected tests (Cp09 per-city sequence, Cp14 membership number, Cp16 city prefix).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format in `assignCustomerCode` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n- **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `city`\n- **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- **NNNN** \u2014 a 4-digit zero-padded sequence that is now **per-city** (one more than the owners already in that city, matched case-insensitively) rather than a global count\n\nThe **membership number** and any other value derived from the customer code are rebuilt automatically: `assignMembershipNumber` already reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` and runs after `assignCustomerCode`, so it now produces `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>-M<YY>` with no additional change needed. I also updated the method's Javadoc to describe the new format.",
